steps.message:
The bug was that `Progress.stop()` was printing a blank line on non-interactive consoles even when `disable=True` was set. I added a check for `self.disable` in the `stop` method to ensure it behaves symmetrically to the `start` method.

```python
    def stop(self) -> None:
        """Stop the progress display."""
        if not self.disable:
            self.live.stop()
            if not self.console.is_interactive and not self.console.is_jupyter:
                self.console.print()
